WEBVTT

00:02.560 --> 00:05.530
In matters relating
to the world of the dead

00:05.630 --> 00:08.990
there is an institution that judges
the sins of the deceased

00:09.250 --> 00:10.790
the Ju-Oh-Cho.

00:11.630 --> 00:13.400
The Summons Section
of the Judgment Bureau

00:13.500 --> 00:17.230
comprises a group supporting
the ministry's operating functions

00:17.340 --> 00:20.170
by guiding the lost souls
that wander the mortal world.

00:20.540 --> 00:22.170
They are also known as...

00:22.410 --> 00:24.850
the Shinigami.

00:25.110 --> 00:31.780
nureta hitomi no oku

00:25.110 --> 00:31.780
Deep behind its wavering stare

00:33.490 --> 00:43.800
aoi tsuki wa shizuka ni koboreochiteyuku

00:33.490 --> 00:43.800
The pale moon quietly descends

00:33.570 --> 00:42.820
Yami no Matsuei

00:50.110 --> 00:55.980
azayaka na sekai wa

00:50.110 --> 00:55.980
The splendid world

00:58.350 --> 01:08.420
oto mo naku shizuka ni yami ni kieteyuku

00:58.350 --> 01:08.420
Disappears into the darkness without a sound

01:08.520 --> 01:16.160
byouyomi no naka kakemeguru yami no naka o

01:08.520 --> 01:16.160
Running about in the dark as time runs out

01:16.260 --> 01:22.790
soshite aratanaru toki o mukae ima

01:16.260 --> 01:22.790
A new era beckons now

01:25.510 --> 01:30.600
kizutsuita kuroi tsubasa

01:25.510 --> 01:30.600
The injured black wings

01:30.780 --> 01:37.150
tsuki no akari ni terasarete

01:30.780 --> 01:37.150
Shine in the moonlight

01:37.750 --> 01:41.950
utsukushiku maiagare

01:37.750 --> 01:41.950
Rising upward in a beautiful dance

01:42.090 --> 01:47.290
shinku no kuchizuke ga ima

01:42.090 --> 01:47.290
The crimson kiss

01:47.400 --> 01:54.230
kokoro no oku ni nagarekomu

01:47.400 --> 01:54.230
Flows deeply into the soul

01:54.400 --> 02:00.200
soshite yume no naka e

01:54.400 --> 02:00.200
Penetrating into one's dreams

02:10.070 --> 02:12.590
There's a small scratch on the cornea.

02:12.700 --> 02:14.730
This is probably the contract.

02:16.880 --> 02:19.500
Huh? Wh-What is this?

02:19.610 --> 02:22.010
The one who has entered into this contract

02:22.110 --> 02:26.070
shall gain stature as a violinist
under the mark of the devil.

02:26.190 --> 02:29.020
In exchange, when the
contractor's goal is attained

02:29.120 --> 02:33.680
he shall hand over the life
of his daughter to me.

02:34.490 --> 02:36.020
By daughter, does he mean--

02:36.130 --> 02:39.290
Normally this contract
would have been fulfilled

02:39.400 --> 02:41.990
when Otonashi Tatsuya
died accidentally.

02:42.100 --> 02:45.300
However, because his cornea
which serves as the contract

02:45.400 --> 02:47.770
was transplanted to Hijiri...

02:47.870 --> 02:52.240
Otonashi Tatsuya has, in a
strange sense, continued to live.

02:52.340 --> 02:56.540
This devil will have to
fulfill the contract again.

02:57.150 --> 03:01.980
The devil wouldn't accept
anything less reasonable.

03:02.390 --> 03:03.750
That's right.

03:03.860 --> 03:07.620
Hijiri's life is actually in danger.
He was even induced to commit suicide.

03:07.730 --> 03:10.190
The devil wants to kill Hijiri

03:10.300 --> 03:13.990
and eliminate Otonashi Tatsuya,
who continues to live within Hijiri.

03:14.100 --> 03:17.190
Then the contract will be fulfilled.

03:20.030 --> 03:25.030
Episode 5: Devil's Trill, Part 2

03:27.150 --> 03:31.580
To think the transplanted cornea
contained a devil's contract...

03:32.020 --> 03:34.610
It's like a really sick joke.

03:34.720 --> 03:35.690
I know!

03:35.790 --> 03:38.650
How about having another operation
and get another cornea?

03:38.760 --> 03:39.880
Forget it.

03:39.990 --> 03:42.360
The moment the cornea was
transplanted into the kid

03:42.460 --> 03:43.930
he became the contractor.

03:44.030 --> 03:45.930
- Yeah, yeah.
- Oh, right.

03:46.030 --> 03:47.970
There's no point
unless we get to the root.

03:48.070 --> 03:51.900
We have a chance of fighting him
if we can figure out his identity.

03:52.000 --> 03:54.170
We're checking into different areas--

03:54.270 --> 03:57.330
But we can't seem to put a finger on it.

03:58.180 --> 04:01.040
Hey, don't worry.
It'll all work out.

04:01.150 --> 04:03.810
You can be sure that we'll protect you.

04:03.920 --> 04:05.780
Right, Hisoka?

04:07.020 --> 04:09.490
Sorry, but I can't agree with that.

04:10.390 --> 04:14.550
I'm not one to say that when push
comes to shove, we'll manage.

04:15.190 --> 04:18.890
I can understand you
wanting to reassure Hijiri.

04:19.000 --> 04:23.490
But who's the one who's
going to suffer when you can't?

04:23.600 --> 04:26.330
Kindness can be a weakness too.

04:26.970 --> 04:29.600
Well, I have an appointment with Boss.

04:32.680 --> 04:34.200
He's awfully uptight.

04:34.310 --> 04:37.610
D-Don't worry about what
he just said, Hijiri-san!

04:44.620 --> 04:45.720
Hi.

04:45.820 --> 04:47.450
Tatsumi-san.

04:47.560 --> 04:51.760
Well? Are you getting a little
used to the Shinigami job?

04:51.860 --> 04:54.160
I don't really understand it yet.

04:54.270 --> 04:56.930
I understand you're learning
a few tricks from Boss.

04:57.040 --> 05:02.270
There's no point in a Shinigami
not being able to use spells.

05:02.370 --> 05:05.100
And I want to be in an
equal position with Tsuzuki.

05:05.480 --> 05:08.780
Don't you think he's too kind for a Shinigami?

05:08.880 --> 05:11.640
An irresponsible sort of kindness.

05:12.750 --> 05:15.720
He may seem a little over-the-top.

05:15.820 --> 05:19.380
But, in his own way,
he's always very serious.

05:19.490 --> 05:21.890
There's no deceit in what he says.

05:21.990 --> 05:23.150
Tatsumi-san...

05:23.530 --> 05:26.430
I know that you'll do well
working with Tsuzuki-san.

05:26.530 --> 05:28.360
I'll guarantee it.

05:28.470 --> 05:29.630
See you.

05:33.910 --> 05:36.930
Serious in his own way, huh?

05:37.810 --> 05:42.080
Anyway, Hijiri, I don't want you
wandering around outside.

05:42.180 --> 05:45.480
There's no way of knowing when
the devil will come after you.

05:45.850 --> 05:48.080
You and Kazusa will stay here at the Ju-Oh-Cho.

05:48.190 --> 05:49.620
That would be the safest.

05:49.720 --> 05:53.750
Wait a minute! Are you saying
I have to stay here the whole time?

05:53.860 --> 05:55.720
Until I'm released from the devil's contract?!

05:55.830 --> 05:57.800
You could say that.

05:57.900 --> 05:59.260
You've got to be kidding!

05:59.360 --> 06:02.270
That would be like just
running away from the devil.

06:02.370 --> 06:05.000
Besides, I have a concert coming up.

06:05.100 --> 06:08.370
I can't just be hiding out here!

06:08.870 --> 06:10.840
Wh-Where are you going?!

06:10.940 --> 06:13.270
- I'm going home.
- What?!

06:13.450 --> 06:16.470
Whatever the devil has up his sleeve,
I won't be defeated.

06:16.580 --> 06:18.450
I'll be sure to survive.

06:18.550 --> 06:20.850
You can't handle it.
You're up against--

06:20.950 --> 06:23.510
I don't know that until I try!

06:26.390 --> 06:28.620
If that's how you feel,
there's no stopping you.

06:28.730 --> 06:30.130
Do what you will.

06:30.230 --> 06:32.290
T-Tsuzuki-san?

06:34.970 --> 06:36.810
Infirmary Room

07:23.080 --> 07:24.670
Hijiri!

07:25.650 --> 07:26.840
Hisoka!

07:33.560 --> 07:34.820
I-I can't believe this.

07:34.930 --> 07:38.690
It seems the devil's going all out now.

07:39.560 --> 07:41.030
Thanks, Hisoka.

07:41.130 --> 07:43.470
We could've been in big
trouble if it weren't for you.

07:43.570 --> 07:44.630
Just doing my job.

07:44.740 --> 07:47.100
T-Tsuzuki, you're injured!

07:48.340 --> 07:52.040
This'll heal quickly.
I am a Shinigami after all.

07:52.910 --> 07:54.110
It's true.

07:54.210 --> 07:56.840
Anyway, I hope you realize it now.

07:56.950 --> 08:00.820
That you can't fight the devil
just because you think you can.

08:01.850 --> 08:04.010
If you die, Kazusa will die too.

08:05.190 --> 08:08.560
If you want to protect Kazusa,
you will listen to what we say.

08:10.360 --> 08:11.830
All right.

08:17.940 --> 08:19.370
Can't do it.

08:19.700 --> 08:24.230
All this work and I still can't
figure out his form or identity.

08:24.440 --> 08:26.210
This devil is a pretty tricky one.

08:26.550 --> 08:29.480
But your face is beaming with pride.

08:29.580 --> 08:32.380
You're actually happy this is a tough opponent.

08:32.480 --> 08:34.040
Can you tell?

08:34.520 --> 08:37.080
I'm taking this as a challenge to me!

08:37.190 --> 08:39.050
I'm not going to lose!

08:40.260 --> 08:43.060
Let's get Kazusa and return
to the Ju-Oh-Cho for now.

08:43.160 --> 08:44.990
- All right?
- Sure.

08:46.630 --> 08:47.830
Hi-chan!

08:48.700 --> 08:51.330
Thank goodness.
You were safe.

08:51.440 --> 08:52.460
Sure.

08:52.570 --> 08:55.440
Hi-chan, is this old man your friend?

08:56.940 --> 08:58.100
Old man?!

08:58.410 --> 09:00.070
Uh, yeah.

09:00.180 --> 09:01.980
So you don't have to worry.

09:05.280 --> 09:06.910
Hey, Hi-chan...

09:07.020 --> 09:09.350
are you angry about the other day?

09:10.290 --> 09:14.090
You came to see me,
but I hid from you, right?

09:15.130 --> 09:19.320
There was something really
scary standing behind you.

09:19.700 --> 09:21.130
Something scary?

09:21.500 --> 09:24.660
So it wasn't because
I didn't like you anymore.

09:25.640 --> 09:27.570
Okay. Thank you.

09:27.670 --> 09:31.370
It looks like that girl saw something.

09:31.480 --> 09:34.500
Yeah. We'll have to look into this.

09:35.380 --> 09:36.750
That's it for now.

09:37.020 --> 09:39.480
I just have my sheet music and violin left.

09:39.580 --> 09:42.140
Just bring as little as you have to.

09:42.250 --> 09:43.380
Right.

09:43.490 --> 09:47.580
Hey, you think Kazusa got
to the Ju-Oh-Cho safely?

09:47.690 --> 09:52.060
Well, Hisoka's with her,
so I don't think we have to worry.

09:52.160 --> 09:53.530
I guess.

09:53.630 --> 09:54.890
Hijiri...

09:55.000 --> 09:58.130
would you mind having a
taste of my special curry rice?

09:58.240 --> 10:00.200
I hope you like it.

10:00.310 --> 10:01.900
Sure. Why not?

10:03.710 --> 10:05.230
Well? Well?

10:05.510 --> 10:08.070
Oh? So good that you're speechless?

10:08.180 --> 10:09.700
That doesn't surprise me.

10:09.810 --> 10:12.840
I used my special spices for this after all.

10:13.390 --> 10:16.720
Hang in there.
It'll be ready in just a little while.

10:18.890 --> 10:22.550
The Shinigami has dead taste buds.

10:22.660 --> 10:24.420
Where're my mints? My mints...

10:24.530 --> 10:28.930
Anyway, I'd better get used to
my new violin before the concert.

10:29.030 --> 10:30.090
I'm counting on you.

11:06.100 --> 11:08.970
You want that violin, don't you?

11:09.070 --> 11:11.840
It is a part of your body.

11:11.940 --> 11:15.710
Without it, you cannot live.

11:16.080 --> 11:20.140
Now, I'll lead you to it.
To the violin.

11:20.750 --> 11:25.450
And you shall play it to your heart's desire.

11:25.560 --> 11:29.290
I will grant you all of the glory and prosperity

11:29.390 --> 11:32.690
and the comfort that you desire.

11:35.470 --> 11:38.440
It's ready, Hijiri!

11:39.670 --> 11:40.640
Hijiri?

11:41.740 --> 11:43.230
Hijiri?

11:43.680 --> 11:45.070
Damn!

11:55.050 --> 11:56.520
I've found it.

12:09.700 --> 12:10.930
Shit!

12:17.340 --> 12:18.400
Hijiri!

12:33.460 --> 12:37.960
Yami no Matsuei

12:53.510 --> 12:54.840
You all right?

12:55.880 --> 12:57.440
Did I--

13:00.420 --> 13:01.940
Did I play it again?

13:02.050 --> 13:03.280
Yeah.

13:03.490 --> 13:04.610
I'm sorry.

13:05.320 --> 13:08.780
Those people who are entranced
by it lose their free will.

13:09.690 --> 13:11.360
Damn!

13:11.460 --> 13:13.690
I guess the devil knows my weakness.

13:13.800 --> 13:17.170
I can't stand being taken
advantage of like this!

13:17.640 --> 13:18.930
Hijiri.

13:20.840 --> 13:22.200
Tsuzuki.

13:23.910 --> 13:25.000
I have a favor to ask.

13:27.410 --> 13:29.780
That's strange.

13:30.650 --> 13:35.020
It's unusual that I can't figure out its
identity after this much searching.

13:35.420 --> 13:38.720
Maybe it's some new kind of devil.

13:38.920 --> 13:40.620
Don't be ridiculous.

13:43.630 --> 13:46.150
I've seen this doggy before.

13:47.570 --> 13:50.060
It was standing behind Hi-chan the other day.

13:50.170 --> 13:51.800
What?! This?!

13:52.800 --> 13:54.930
We're in for big trouble!

13:56.440 --> 13:57.530
Tsuzuki!

14:01.980 --> 14:04.070
Where are you going, Hi-chan?

14:04.280 --> 14:08.340
I promised you that I'd play
the violin for you, right?

14:08.450 --> 14:11.250
I am to carry out that promise.

14:51.630 --> 14:53.430
Watch it, Hi-chan!

15:01.070 --> 15:02.540
So we finally meet.

15:02.640 --> 15:04.670
I was getting tired of waiting, Devil-san.

15:08.150 --> 15:10.170
Come this way, Hijiri-san!

15:10.280 --> 15:12.880
Damn. A Shinigami, huh?

15:12.980 --> 15:17.550
You were so good at hiding
that I thought I'd invite you instead.

15:17.860 --> 15:20.880
To Minase Hijiri's midnight concert.

15:21.530 --> 15:22.520
I see.

15:22.630 --> 15:27.460
But you all will regret
that you lured me out.

15:27.570 --> 15:28.960
Right now.

15:37.840 --> 15:40.680
- What the hell is that?!
- We're up against a big one.

15:41.180 --> 15:44.170
That's Sargatanas, the leader
of the spirit wanderers

15:44.280 --> 15:47.180
follower of the great ruler
of the netherworld, Astaroth.

15:47.290 --> 15:50.780
To think a day would come
when I'd actually meet him.

15:58.530 --> 16:01.020
If you people had not
interfered in the first place,

16:01.130 --> 16:04.660
I could have finished the
kid off with the violin.

16:05.540 --> 16:07.530
I have no other choice now.

16:08.040 --> 16:10.410
First I will have to destroy the kid

16:10.510 --> 16:13.170
and then I will take the little girl.

16:30.900 --> 16:32.490
I-Incredible!

16:32.960 --> 16:35.630
That's the leader of the
spirit wanderers for you.

16:36.070 --> 16:38.190
- T-Tsuzuki!
- Don't worry.

16:38.300 --> 16:41.300
Hisoka, Watari. You guys
take care of Hijiri and Kazusa.

16:41.410 --> 16:42.740
Right. Leave them to us!

16:42.840 --> 16:45.310
You're not getting away!

16:50.750 --> 16:54.240
I bow to thee and beseech you.
The Twelve Gods that protect me.

16:54.350 --> 16:57.840
The sword of heaven, the living steel
of nothingness, in the silver tusk.

16:57.960 --> 17:00.550
Appear before me!

17:04.600 --> 17:05.990
Byakko!

17:21.450 --> 17:23.880
You worthless insects!

17:39.930 --> 17:43.370
W-We've been saved, Hisoka.

17:44.040 --> 17:45.470
Pretty incredible.

17:45.570 --> 17:48.060
Even though he's just
borrowing the powers

17:48.170 --> 17:50.900
he's actually well matched
against Sargatanas.

17:51.180 --> 17:52.140
Tsuzuki.

17:55.310 --> 17:56.870
- What's the matter?!
- Hi-chan!

17:56.980 --> 17:58.740
My eye!

18:08.590 --> 18:09.790
Tsuzuki!

18:10.600 --> 18:11.720
Hijiri!

18:15.700 --> 18:16.830
Tsuzuki!

18:17.200 --> 18:19.190
I'll rip your arms off!

18:20.540 --> 18:22.030
Why, you!

18:22.410 --> 18:23.770
Byakko!

18:30.750 --> 18:32.580
You!

18:42.230 --> 18:43.660
Tsuzuki!

18:45.000 --> 18:46.760
Is everyone all right?

18:46.860 --> 18:49.200
Never mind that.
I just want to see your body!

18:49.870 --> 18:51.960
What are you doing, Watari-san?!

18:52.500 --> 18:53.800
You mustn't do that!

18:53.910 --> 18:57.360
I don't see any sign of it anywhere.
Thank goodness!

18:57.480 --> 19:00.210
There's nothing there!
You can relax!

19:00.310 --> 19:02.610
Watari, is that...

19:03.350 --> 19:06.210
- how you felt about me?
- No, you idiot!

19:06.650 --> 19:09.020
I was just checking to see

19:09.120 --> 19:11.990
if that evil dog planted a parasite in you.

19:12.090 --> 19:13.060
Parasite?

19:13.160 --> 19:14.220
That's right.

19:14.330 --> 19:19.230
When he possesses you, he leaves
a mark where he has bitten you.

19:19.330 --> 19:23.160
Generally most spirits, like devils and angels

19:23.270 --> 19:25.860
don't possess physical forms of their own.

19:26.370 --> 19:28.570
That Sargatanas is a parasitic type

19:28.670 --> 19:31.400
who only exists by taking the form of others.

19:32.610 --> 19:36.510
Well, from what I saw,
there seems to be no sign of it.

19:36.610 --> 19:39.780
You probably blew him away
before he latched on to you.

19:41.320 --> 19:42.810
That's a relief.

19:42.920 --> 19:45.320
Thank goodness everyone's safe.

19:45.420 --> 19:46.390
Tsuzuki!

19:47.430 --> 19:49.260
Maybe you should take it easy for a while.

19:49.360 --> 19:50.830
Don't worry.

19:50.930 --> 19:53.520
A wound like this will heal in no time.

19:53.630 --> 19:54.930
But it must hurt.

19:55.370 --> 19:57.530
Just because you guys are immortal

19:57.640 --> 19:59.760
doesn't mean you should just ignore it.

19:59.900 --> 20:02.900
Do you feel concern for me, Hijiri?

20:03.440 --> 20:04.670
I mean...

20:04.780 --> 20:07.400
if you guys weren't around--

20:07.910 --> 20:11.970
Thank you.
But I'm really okay.

20:14.420 --> 20:17.050
Come on. Don't look so sad.
It doesn't suit you.

20:35.470 --> 20:38.100
You must have suffered,
you little insect.

20:38.210 --> 20:41.510
You! You're still alive!

20:41.610 --> 20:44.880
You mustn't underestimate
the power of the devil.

20:48.120 --> 20:50.140
The part that I bit will start to hurt.

20:50.250 --> 20:51.520
Stop!

20:52.320 --> 20:56.990
That is because I am entering you,
each and every cell in you.

20:57.090 --> 20:59.220
No! Get out of me!

20:59.330 --> 21:00.800
I can't do that.

21:00.900 --> 21:03.800
I've finally found myself
a new host after all.

21:04.200 --> 21:08.000
Look, my mark will soon reveal itself on you.

21:10.580 --> 21:13.170
Of the black sheep.

21:14.580 --> 21:17.610
The mark that turns its back on God.

21:19.050 --> 21:21.080
You should feel lucky

21:21.190 --> 21:26.210
that you were chosen
to become a part of my body.

21:31.660 --> 21:33.930
Poor little lamb.

21:39.960 --> 21:42.960
Next Episode

21:41.870 --> 21:43.570
Hijiri's back to normal

21:43.670 --> 21:45.200
and the crime has been solved.

21:45.310 --> 21:47.830
How about getting Boss some
spicy squid as a souvenir?

21:47.950 --> 21:51.850
What do you mean?
Boss has a sweet tooth, if anything.

21:52.380 --> 21:54.370
Don't talk to me about sweet things.

21:54.490 --> 21:56.210
I have a weakness for it.

21:56.320 --> 21:59.150
What? Hey, Tsuzuki.
What's the matter?

22:00.860 --> 22:05.230
Next time on Yami no Matsuei: The Devil's Trill, Part 3

22:00.980 --> 22:09.910
Episode 6          Devil's Trill, Part 3

22:05.560 --> 22:09.190
Those who live in the darkness wander aimlessly.

22:18.230 --> 22:21.590
arumikan no marui en o mashikaku ni orinagara

22:18.230 --> 22:21.590
As I square the round edges on the drink

22:21.700 --> 22:24.630
kimi o matsu machikado sa

22:21.700 --> 22:24.630
I wait for you on the street corner

22:24.730 --> 22:28.220
nakami no ekitai wa mou nurukute nomenai kedo

22:24.730 --> 22:28.220
The liquid inside is warm and I can't drink it anymore

22:28.340 --> 22:30.930
shikatanaku motsu ore sa

22:28.340 --> 22:30.930
But what can I do but hold onto to it?

22:31.040 --> 22:38.270
yami no naka de ore o utsusu
garasu keesu ni kazarareta

22:31.040 --> 22:38.270
In the glass case reflecting me in the darkness

22:38.380 --> 22:45.010
ningyou ga sakki kara kowai
kao de ore o miteru

22:38.380 --> 22:45.010
There is a doll that has been scowling at me

22:58.470 --> 23:04.890
ore no fuku kuchibue wa wari
to akarui uta de

22:58.470 --> 23:04.890
The tune I whistle is a bright and cheerful one

